.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
rmdir
- remove directories
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
rmdir directory ...
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Rmdir removes each named directory, which must be empty.  The entry is
removed from its parent, then the two entries every directory carries -
"." pointing at itself and ".." at the parent - are unlinked, so the
directory's inode is freed.
.sp
Micronix has no rmdir system call.  The directory is removed the way
rm -d removes one, and - as with rm -d - only the super-user can do it.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
mkdir (1), rm (1)
